id:                     E419
trigger_tool:           clang|autotools|conan
phase:                  testing|runtime
error_signature:        expected.*-[0-9]+.*actual.*[12][0-9]{2}|INT8.*char|plain char.*unsigned

severity:               2
category:               abi, c-language, signedness
match_keywords:         -fsigned-char, plain char, unsigned char, INT8, integer promotion, AArch64, pixel sample
title:                  Target plain-char signedness can change INT8 API results without changing stored bytes

root_cause:             C leaves plain char signedness implementation-defined. A target compiler may default plain char to unsigned while upstream code uses char variables and char pointers as signed 8-bit samples. The stored byte remains unchanged, but integer promotion turns values such as -120 and -17 into 136 and 239, so comparisons and API results fail only on the target.
affected_scope:         C libraries that use plain char rather than signed char or int8_t for semantically signed 8-bit samples, especially image, raster, codec, audio, and binary-format code built for a target whose plain-char default differs from upstream test hosts.
verification_cmd:       Confirm the failing values differ by 256; audit the upstream declaration and API output type; rebuild every affected C object with -fsigned-char; run the complete unchanged upstream suite and package consumer on the real target.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           consistent-target-signed-char-mode
rec_description:        When the upstream source and public API intentionally use plain char for signed 8-bit values, add -fsigned-char through the package toolchain so every affected C translation unit uses one consistent semantic mode. Preserve upstream source and test expectations, and verify the full target suite.
rec_command:            toolchain.extra_cflags.append("-fsigned-char")
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-toolchain

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      upstream-explicit-signed-type
fallback_description:   If upstream accepts an API or source correction, replace semantic INT8 declarations with signed char or int8_t consistently and review ABI compatibility before backporting.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       expected.*(136|239)|change.*test.*expected|cast.*test.*unsigned
forbid_1_reason:        Rewriting expected results or casting only in tests hides the target semantic mismatch and does not repair library API behavior.
forbid_1_consequence:   The suite can become falsely green while downstream callers still receive unsigned-promoted values.
forbid_2_pattern:       __OHOS__|OHOS.*ifdef|HarmonyOS.*ifdef
forbid_2_reason:        The issue is a compiler plain-char mode and should be expressed through the toolchain for all affected translation units, not an operating-system source macro.
forbid_2_consequence:   Conditional source forks obscure ABI intent and can leave different library objects compiled with inconsistent signedness.

principles:             P005,P013
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

